> payout 100 (full minus deductible, no special clause)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon sword ench5 damage 800 -> payout 700 (dragon full, then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"steel sword ench9 damage 1000 -> payout 400 (high-enchantment 50%, then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon sword ench9 damage 1000 -> payout 400 (both clauses, 50% wins)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon sword ench8 damage 1000 -> payout 400 (threshold, 50% then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon attack: sword 500 + amulet 300 -> payout 600 (deductible per damaged item)\");\n  it.todo(\"two swords both damaged -> each entry its own deductible\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - cap exhaustion across successive claims\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"sword cap 2000, two 1500-claims -> first payout 1400 (remaining 600), second 600 (remaining 0)\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - error handling (CLI non-zero exit)\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"quote with unknown item type throws\");\n  it.todo(\"claim references item not in policy throws\");\n  it.todo(\"claim has more damage entries of a type than covered throws\");\n  it.todo(\"claim damage amount negative throws\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - full scenario processing\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"schema example: quote then claim returns premium, payout, remainingCap\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784906957518},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see that only `basePremium` has been implemented while the others are still stubs, so let me run the tests to check the current state.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_012Av5YaMZzNpVn56n6hik1Y","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-3 && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -15"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":2260,"output":168,"cacheRead":9886,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning"