4 passing.\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent):** Names are clear; the comment documents extension policy. No improvement found that increases clarity.\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication):** The 4 stubs share the `undefined as unknown as number` cast — but these are TDD placeholders, not real logic. Extracting a shared stub helper would *add* an abstraction (worsening Rule 4) and obscure that each is a to-be-implemented function. The one real function (`basePremium`) has no duplication.\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements):** `basePremium` is a single-expression lookup — already minimal. No unnecessary abstraction.\n\n### Step 4-6: Decision\n\n**Refactoring Evaluation — the implemented code (`basePremium` + lookup table):**\n\nThe only tested, non-stub code is already optimal:\n1. **Naming:** `basePremium` and `basePremiumByType` clearly reveal intent.\n2. **Duplication:** None in real logic. The repeated cast lives only in stubs that will be replaced by upcoming Red/Green cycles; touching them now would add churn and risk masking future compile-time signals.\n3. **Mass:** 9 — minimal for a table-driven lookup. Converting to a `switch`/conditionals would *raise* mass (each `case` ≈ conditional) and hurt clarity.\n4. **Fewest elements:** Single expression, no extra abstraction.\n\nI attempted improvements against all four rules and found that any change (extracting stub casts, replacing the lookup with control flow, renaming) would either **worsen mass**, **reduce clarity**, or **prematurely alter TDD stubs**. Therefore no change was applied to the tested code.\n\nLet me confirm tests remain green (no changes made, so state is preserved):"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_019BC64XKRE4XAM9bxREb4Du","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-3 && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -6"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"in