efactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Functions insuranceSum, capFor, roundPremium, roundPayout, processScenario are still stubs.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":1147,"output":361,"cacheRead":68705,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":70213,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784907766954,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-d35a13bc-4f9b-45c0-b990-33bafe23d54f","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_014aZeJpWnmhFpmxU8cJZtZ4","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 17 tests remain green.\n\n### Step 5: Refactored Code Mass\n```\nconst policyWideRate = ({ yearsWithMHPCO }: QuoteInput): number =>\n  FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE - (yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD ? LOYALTY_DISCOUNT : 0);\n\nexport const quote = (input: QuoteInput): number => {\n  const policyBase = basePremium(input.items);\n  return policyBase + itemSurcharges(input.items) + policyBase * policyWideRate(input) + PROCESSING_FEE;\n};\n```\n- `policyWideRate`: bindings 3, conditional 1 (=4) → **7**\n- `quote`: bindings ~8, invocations 4 (=8), constant 0 → **~16**\n- **Total Mass: ~23** (down from 38, delta −15)\n\nThe conditional count dropped from being duplicated in an amount context; the two independent `policyBase * rate` amounts collapsed into a single `policyBase * policyWideRate(input)` term.\n\n## Refactoring Report\n\n**Refactoring Applied**: Extracted `policyWideRate(input)` — the net sum of all policy-level rate modifiers (first-insurance surcharge minus loyalty discount), applied once to `policyBase`.\n\n- **Naming**: `quote` kept (accurate). New `policyWideRate` names the previously-implicit \"policy-wide modifiers\" concept, mirroring the existing per-item `surchargeRateForItem`.\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: The policy-wide side now uses the same summed-rate pattern as the per-item side, making the two modifier families structurally parallel and self-documenting.\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication)**: Removed the conceptual duplication of two separate `policyBase * rate` amount calculations; they're now one term.\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements)**: Eliminated the `firstInsurance` and `loyalty` intermediate bindings.\n\n**Extensibility benefit**: The upcoming follow-up-contract 15% discount becomes a single additional signed term inside `policyWideRate`, with no change to `quote`'s return expression — exactly the \"add more policy-wide modifiers cleanly\" goal noted in the task.\n\n**Mass Change**: ~38 → ~23 (delta −15)\n**Tests**: All 17 passing (23 todo untouched); stubs `insuranceSum`, `capFor`, `roundPremium`, `roundPayout`, `processScenario` left as-is per their pending tests."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-3/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 17\nRecent Green phase: quote now subtracts a loyalty discount (20% of policy base) when yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD=2.\n\nNote: upcoming tests add a follow-up-contract 15% discount (policy-wide) and combined-modifier integration cases. Do not implement ahead, but keep quote cleanly structured so more policy-wide modifiers can be added.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Functions insuranceSum, capFor, roundPremium, roundPayout, processScenario are still stubs.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 17\nRecent Green phase: quote now subtracts a loyalty discount (20% of policy base) when yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD=2.\n\nNote: upcoming tests add a follow-up-contract 15% discount (policy-wide) and combined-modifier integration cases. Do not implement ahead, but keep quote cleanly structured so more policy-wide modifiers can be added.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Functions insuranceSum, capFor, roundPremium, roundPayout, processScenario are still stubs.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784907772662},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'll start by reading the implementation and test files to understand the current state."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_013YwxpQRkDujAAKMyJUSsKp","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-3/src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01Q7Pr7SCNGGXcU9NhcGiQwx","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-3/src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":328,"output":258,"cacheRead":9696,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10282,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784907772681,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-893c6e85-0eb9-4eb0-afaf-ee8f7bc567e4","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_013YwxpQRkDujAAKMyJUSsKp","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// MHPCO price list: base premium in gold per item type.\n// Extend this table as new item types are covered by tests.\nconst basePremiumByType: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\ntype Item = { type: string; material?: string; enchantment?: number; cursed?: boolean };\n\n// A \"building block\" of components earns a discounted flat base premium\n// instead of the sum of its parts.\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst basePremiumForItem = (item: Item): number => basePremiumByType[item.type];\n\nconst sumOfItemPremiums = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, one) => sum + basePremiumForItem(one), 0);\n\n// A block is exactly BLOCK_SIZE components that are all the same type.\nconst isBlockOfAlikeComponents = (items: Item[]): boolean =>\n  items.length === BLOCK_SIZE &&\n  items.every((one) => one.type === items[0].type);\n\nconst premiumForGroup = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  isBlockOfAlikeComponents(items) ? BLOCK_BASE_PREMIUM : sumOfItemPremiums(items);\n\nconst groupByType = (items: Item[]): Item[][] => {\n  const byType = new Map<string, Item[]>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    const group = byType.get(item.type) ?? [];\n    group.push(item);\n    byType.set(item.type, group);\n  }\n  return [...byType.values()];\n};\n\nexport const basePremium = (itemOrItems: Item | Item[]): number => {\n  if (!Array.isArray(itemOrItems)) return basePremiumForItem(itemOrItems);\n  return groupByType(itemOrItems).reduce(\n    (total, group) => total + premiumForGroup(group),\n    0,\n  );\n};\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\ntype QuoteInput = {\n  items: Item[];\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n  isFollowUpContract: boolean;\n};\n\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE = 0.1;\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\n\n// The total surcharge rate is the sum of every applicable per-item modifier.\n// Add new item modifiers (e.g. high-enchantment) as further terms here.\nconst isHighEnchantment = (item: Item): boolean =>\n  (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD;\n\nconst surchargeRateForItem = (item: Item): number =>\n  (item.cursed ? CURSE_SURCHARGE : 0) +\n  (isHighEnchantment(item) ? HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE : 0);\n\nconst surchargeForItem = (item: Item): number =>\n  basePremiumForItem(item) * surchargeRateForItem(item);\n\nconst itemSurcharges = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, one) => sum + surchargeForItem(one), 0);\n\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\n\nexport const quote = ({ items, yearsWithMHPCO }: QuoteInput): number => {\n  const policyBase = basePremium(items);\n  const firstInsurance = policyBase * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE;\n  const loyalty =\n    yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD ? policyBase * LOYALTY_DISCOUNT : 0;\n  return (\n    policyBase + itemSurcharges(items) + firstInsurance - loyalty + PROCESSING_FEE\n  );\n};\n\nexport const insuranceSum = (items: unknown): number => {\n  return undefined as unknown as number;\n};\n\nexport const capFor = (items: unknown): number => {\n  return undefined as unknown as number;\n};\n\nexport const roundPremium = (amount: number): number => {\n  return undefined as unknown as number;\n};\n\nexport const roundPayout = (amount: number): number => {\n  return undefined as unknown as number;\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (input: unknown): unknown => {\n  return undefined;\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784907775938},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01Q7Pr7SCNGGXcU9NhcGiQwx","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport {\n  basePremium,\n  quote,\n  insuranceSum,\n  capFor,\n  roundPremium,\n  roundPayout,\n  processScenario,\n} from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - base premiums (price list)\", () => {\n  it(\"sword base premium is 100 G\", () => {\n    expect(basePremium({ type: \"sword\" })).toBe(100);\n  });\n  it(\"amulet base premium is 60 G\", () => {\n    expect(basePremium({ type: \"amulet\" })).toBe(60);\n  });\n  it(\"staff base premium is 80 G\", () => {\n    expect(basePremium({ type: \"staff\" })).toBe(80);\n  });\n  it(\"potion base premium is 40 G\", () => {\n    expect(basePremium({ type: \"potion\" })).toBe(40);\n  });\n  it(\"single component (rune) base premium is 25 G\", () => {\n    expect(basePremium({ type: \"rune\" })).toBe(25);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - building blocks of alike components\", () => {\n  it(\"2 runes -> 50 G base premium\", () => {\n    expect(basePremium([{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }])).toBe(50);\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes -> 60 G base premium (block applies)\", () => {\n    expect(basePremium([{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }])).toBe(60);\n  });\n  it(\"4 runes -> 100 G base premium (no block, requires exactly 3)\", () => {\n    expect(basePremium([{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }])).toBe(100);\n  });\n  it(\"7 runes -> 175 G base premium (no block)\", () => {\n    expect(basePremium(Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" })))).toBe(175);\n  });\n  it(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone -> 75 G base premium (no block: different types)\", () => {\n    expect(basePremium([{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }])).toBe(75);\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones -> 120 G base premium (two separate blocks)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      basePremium([\n        { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" },\n        { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" },\n      ]),\n    ).toBe(120);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - quote premium modifiers and fee\", () => {\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only processing fee)\", () => {\n    expect(quote({ items: [], yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false })).toBe(5);\n  });\n  it(\"single sword, newcomer first quote -> 115 G (100 + 10 first + 5 fee)\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote({ items: [{ type: \"sword\" }], yearsWithMHPCO: 0, isFollowUpContract: false }),\n    ).toBe(115);\n  });\n  it(\"cursed items add 50% surcharge: newcomer cursed sword ench3 -> 165 G\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote({\n        items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true }],\n        yearsWithMHPCO: 0,\n        isFollowUpContract: false,\n      }),\n    ).toBe(165);\n  });\n  it(\"high enchantment (>=5) adds 30%: newcomer sword ench5 -> 145 G\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote({\n        items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 5, cursed: false }],\n        yearsWithMHPCO: 0,\n        isFollowUpContract: false,\n      }),\n    ).toBe(145);\n  });\n  it(\"enchantment 4 -> no high-enchantment surcharge: newcomer sword ench4 -> 115 G\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote({\n        items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 4, cursed: false }],\n        yearsWithMHPCO: 0,\n        isFollowUpContract: false,\n      }),\n    ).toBe(115);\n  });\n  it(\"loyalty discount (exactly 2 years) applies 20%: sword ench3 -> 95 G\", () => {\n    expect(\n      quote({\n        items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }],\n        yearsWithMHPCO: 2,\n        isFollowUpContract: false,\n      }),\n    ).toBe(95);\n  });\n  it.todo(\"long-standing second contract cursed sword ench7 -> 160 G (all modifiers stack)\");\n  it.todo(\"multi-item scope: cursed surcharge is 50% of cursed item base, not policy total -> 231 G\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - rounding in MHPCO's favor\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"premium 197.5 G -> 198 G (rounded up)\");\n  it.todo(\"payout 350.5 G -> 350 G (rounded down)\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - insurance sum and cap\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"two swords -> insurance sum 2000 G\");\n  it.todo(\"sword + amulet -> insurance sum 1600 G\");\n  it.todo(\"sword + 3 runes block -> insurance sum 1750 G (block affects premium only)\");\n  it.todo(\"two swords -> cap 4000 G (twice insurance sum)\");\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword -> cap 2000 G (based on unmodified insurance value)\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - claim payout (single claim)\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"regular sword steel ench3 damage 500 -> payout 400 (full minus deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"rune damage 200 -> payout 100 (full minus deductible, no special clause)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon sword ench5 damage 800 -> payout 700 (dragon full, then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"steel sword ench9 damage 1000 -> payout 400 (high-enchantment 50%, then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon sword ench9 damage 1000 -> payout 400 (both clauses, 50% wins)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon sword ench8 damage 1000 -> payout 400 (threshold, 50% then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon attack: sword 500 + amulet 300 -> payout 600 (deductible per damaged item)\");\n  it.todo(\"two swords both damaged -> each entry its own deductible\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - cap exhaustion across successive claims\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"sword cap 2000, two 1500-claims -> first payout 1400 (remaining 600), second 600 (remaining 0)\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - error handling (CLI non-zero exit)\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"quote with unknown item type throws\");\n  it.todo(\"claim references item not in policy throws\");\n  it.todo(\"claim has more damage entries of a type than covered throws\");\n  it.todo(\"claim damage amount negative throws\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - full scenario processing\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"schema example: quote then claim returns premium, payout, remainingCap\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784907775938},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Running the tests to verify everything passes.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01A3nfEoYY4GcwdhutNa1yRV","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-3 && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","us