oring.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"All 18 tests pass. Let me analyze the implementation for refactoring opportunities.\n\n## Refactoring Analysis\n\n### Step 1: Naming Evaluation (FIRST PRIORITY)\n\nI reviewed the recently changed and surrounding code:\n\n- `policyWideRate` — clearly reveals it computes the net policy-level rate. Good.\n- `surchargeRateForItem` / `surchargeForItem` — clear per-item scope. Good.\n- `itemSurcharges` — this is a **sum** over items, but its sibling helper is named `sumOfItemPremiums`. The plural-noun name hides that it aggregates. **Inconsistent naming** with the established `sumOf...` convention.\n- `quote` — accurately names the whole computation, but its body inlines four distinct premium components with no names, hiding the intent of each term.\n\n**Decision:**\n1. Rename `itemSurcharges` → `sumOfItemSurcharges` (consistency with `sumOfItemPremiums`, reveals aggregation).\n2. Introduce explaining variables in `quote` so each premium component is named.\n\n### Step 2: Initial APP Mass — `quote`\n\n```ts\nexport const quote = (input: QuoteInput): number => {\n  const policyBase = basePremium(input.items);\n  return (\n    policyBase + itemSurcharges(input.items) +\n    policyBase * policyWideRate(input) + PROCESSING_FEE\n  );\n};\n```\n\n- Bindings/scalars: `input`(×3), `policyBase`(×3 incl. decl), `PROCESSING_FEE`(×1) = 7 → 7\n- Invocations: `basePremium`, `itemSurcharges`, `policyWideRate` (3) + arithmetic `+`×3, `*`×1 (4) = 7 → 14\n- Conditionals/loops/assignments: 0 (const binding counted as binding)\n\n**Total Mass: 21**\n\n### Step 3–4: Apply Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)\n\nBoth refactorings serve Rule 2. Rule 1 (tests) preserved, Rule 3 (no new duplication), Rule 4 (no new elements beyond named locals that clarify)."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_017oM664kaQzPT9hrDrPJNgr","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"const itemSurcharges = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, one) => sum + surchargeForItem(one), 0);","newText":"const sumOfItemSurcharges = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, one) => sum + surchargeForItem(one), 0);"},{"oldText":"export const quote = (input: QuoteInput): number => {\n  const policyBase = basePremium(input.items);\n  return (\n    policyBase +\n    itemSurcharges(input.items) +\n    policyBase * policyWideRate(input) +\n    PROCESSING_FEE\n  );\n};","newText":"export const quote = (input: QuoteInput): number => {\n  const policyBase = basePremium(input.items);\n  const perItemSurcharges = sumOfItemSurcharges(input.items);\n  const policyWideAdjustment = policyBase * policyWideRate(input);\n  return policyBase + perItemSurcharges + policyWideAdjustment + PROCESSING_FEE;\n};"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":4924,"output":2831,"cacheRead":9978,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":17733,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784907898650,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-e90a5d2e-2d26-4193-91bc-3eeee05935e1","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_017oM664kaQzPT9hrDrPJNgr","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 2 block(s) in src/claim-office.ts."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n  71 \n  72 const surchargeForItem = (item: Item): number =>\n  73   basePremiumForItem(item) * surchargeRateForItem(item);\n  74 \n- 75 const itemSurcharges = (items: Item[]): number =>\n+ 75 const sumOfItemSurcharges = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  76   items.reduce((sum, one) => sum + surchargeForItem(one), 0);\n  77 \n  78 const LOYALTY_DISCOUNT = 0.2;\n  79 const LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\n     ...\n  88   (isFollowUpContract ? FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT : 0);\n  89 \n  90 export const quote = (input: QuoteInput): number => {\n  91   const policyBase = basePremium(input.items);\n- 92  