lication** between the two lookup functions:\n\n```typescript\nconst basePremiumForItem = (item: Item): number => basePremiumByType[item.type];\nconst insuranceValueForItem = (item: Item): number => insuranceValueByType[item.type];\n```\n\nBoth encode the identical knowledge: *\"the value for an item is its type's entry in a per-type table.\"* This is exactly what the Green-phase note points at. I'll extract that shared knowledge into one place.\n\nNote: I deliberately will **not** couple the two tables via the coincidental `insuranceValue = premium × 10` relationship — that ratio is not a stated domain rule, so encoding it would *hurt* Rule 2 (reveal a rule that may not exist) and couple independent price-list facts.\n\n### Step 3: APP Mass (before)\n\n```\nbasePremiumForItem:    bindings item, basePremiumByType, item.type = 3;  index access (invocation) = 2  -> 5\ninsuranceValueForItem: bindings item, insuranceValueByType, item.type = 3; index access = 2            -> 5\nTotal: 10\n```\n\nLet me apply the extraction."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_018jZwez3AFQqdkqCsJscQbL","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"const basePremiumForItem = (item: Item): number => basePremiumByType[item.type];","newText":"// Every per-item value is the item type's entry in a per-type price table.\nconst valueByType = (table: Record<string, number>) => (item: Item): number =>\n  table[item.type];\n\nconst basePremiumForItem = valueByType(basePremiumByType);"},{"oldText":"const insuranceValueForItem = (item: Item): number => insuranceValueByType[item.type];","newText":"const insuranceValueForItem = valueByType(insuranceValueByType);"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":5726,"output":2768,"cacheRead":9696,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":18190,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784908200351,"r