outForDamage`, `reimbursementRateForItem` — all fit their purpose.\n\n**Decision: Keep all names — they clearly reveal intent.**\n\n### Step 2 & 3: Applying Simple Design Rules\n\nThe strongest candidate is the coupling between `matchDamagesToItems` and `totalPayout`. Currently `matchDamagesToItems` returns an `Item[]` that must be **index-aligned** with the `damages` array, and `totalPayout` reaches back in with `matched[i]`:\n\n```ts\nconst matched = matchDamagesToItems(damages, items);\nreturn damages.reduce(\n  (sum, damage, i) => sum + payoutForDamage(damage, matched[i]),\n  0,\n);\n```\n\nThis positional index coupling between two parallel arrays is a **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)** weakness — the relationship between a damage and its matched item is implicit in the shared index. Making the pairing explicit removes the fragile index access.\n\n### Step 2: Initial APP Mass (of the two affected functions)\n\n**`totalPayout` (before):**\n- Bindings: `damages`, `items`, `matched`, `sum`, `damage`, `i` = 6\n- Invocations: `matchDamagesToItems`, `payoutForDamage`, `+`, `matched[i]` = 4 → 8\n- Loops: `reduce` = 5\n- Constants: `0` = 1\n\n**Total: 20**\n\nLet me apply the refactoring:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01SVtcGPSciXPAYcAD3v92Mn","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"// Matches each damage to a distinct covered item of the same type. Throws when a\n// damage has no matching (unused) item, so over-claiming or unknown items are rejected.\nconst matchDamagesToItems = (damages: Damage[], items: Item[]): Item[] => {\n  const available = [...items];\n  return damages.map((damage) => {\n    const index = available.findIndex((one) => one.type === damage.itemType);\n    if (index === -1)\n      throw new Error(`Damage refers to item not covered by policy: ${damage.itemType}`);\n    return available.splice(index, 1)[0];\n  });\n};\n\nconst totalPayout = (damages: Damage[], items: Item[]): number => {\n  const matched = matchDamagesToItems(damages, items);\n  return damages.reduce(\n    (sum, damage, i) => sum + payoutForDamage(damage, matched[i]),\n    0,\n  );\n};","newText":"// A damage paired with the specific covered item it is claimed against.\ntype MatchedDamage = { damage: Damage; item: Item };\n\n// Matches each damage to a distinct covered item of the same type. Throws when a\n// damage has no matching (unused) item, so over-claiming or unknown items are rejected.\nconst matchDamagesToItems = (damages: Damage[], items: Item[]): MatchedDamage[] => {\n  const available = [...items];\n  return damages.map((damage) => {\n    const index = available.findIndex((one) => one.type === damage.itemType);\n    if (index === -1)\n      throw new Error(`Damage refers to item not covered by policy: ${damage.itemType}`);\n    return { damage, item: available.splice(index, 1)[0] };\n  });\n};\n\nconst totalPayout = (damages: Damage[], items: Item[]): number =>\n  matchDamagesToItems(damages, items).reduce(\n    (sum, { damage, item }) => sum + payoutForDamage(damage, item),\n    0,\n  );"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":7946,"output":3961,"cacheRead":9995,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":21902,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784908760630,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-50cd8fea-2638-4358-b5e7-66d8fc8a7aee","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01SVtcGPSciXPAYcAD3v92Mn","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in src/claim-office.ts."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n 154 // clauses) less the deductible.\n 155 const payoutForDamage = (damage: Damage, item: Item): number =>\n 156   damage.amount * reimbursementRateForItem(item) - DEDUCTIBLE;\n 157 \n+158 // A damage paired with the specific covered item it is claimed against.\n+159 type MatchedDamage = { damage: D