mount cannot be negative: ${damage.amount}`);\n  }\n};\n\nconst totalPayout = (damages: Damage[], items: Item[]): number =>\n  matchDamagesToItems(damages, items).reduce(\n    (sum, { damage, item }) => sum + payoutForDamage(damage, item),\n    0,\n  );\n\nexport const claim = (\n  items: Item[],\n\n[13 more lines in file. Use offset=190 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784908914388},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01CbmcCwKr3LcQB9X3zusrQa","name":"read","arguments":{"limit":20,"offset":188,"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-3/src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":1183,"output":162,"cacheRead":118953,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":120298,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784908914392,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-f50b8da9-698b-4260-bd6a-89d3867b7349","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01CbmcCwKr3LcQB9X3zusrQa","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export const claim = (\n  items: Item[],\n  incident: Incident,\n  remainingCap: number = capFor(items),\n): ClaimResult => {\n  assertNonNegativeDamages(incident.damages);\n  const desiredPayout = totalPayout(incident.damages, items);\n  const payout = Math.min(desiredPayout, remainingCap);\n  return { payout, remainingCap: remainingCap - payout };\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (input: unknown): unknown => {\n  return undefined;\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784908917470},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm implementing processScenario to track the remaining cap per policy across multiple claim steps, and I need to make sure the quote gets rounded properly. Looking at the schema example where premium equals 59, the calculation checks out exactly without rounding needed, but I should apply roundPremium anyway. For the claim side, the remaining cap starts at the capFor value for the items, which is 1200.\n\nDefining the types for the scenario...","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now let me implement processScenario. It processes steps sequentially, tracking each policy's items and remaining cap for successive claims."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01PEuQkyNwjugCRqVLkt99s2","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"type QuoteStep = { op: \"quote\"; items: Item[] };\ntype ClaimStep = { op: \"claim\"; policy: number; incident: Incident };\ntype Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\ntype Scenario = { customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number }; steps: Step[] };\ntype StepResult = { premium: number } | ClaimResult;\n\nexport const processScenario = (input: Scenario): { results: StepResult[] } => {\n  const { customer, steps } = input;\n  const policyItems = new Map<number, Item[]>();\n  const remainingCaps = new Map<number, number>();\n  let quoteCount = 0;\n\n  const results = steps.map((step, index): StepResult => {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      policyItems.set(index, step.items);\n      remainingCaps.set(index, capFor(step.items));\n      quoteCount += 1;\n      const premium = quote({\n        items: step.items,\n        yearsWithMHPCO: customer.yearsWithMHPCO,\n        isFollowUpContract: quoteCount > 1,\n      });\n      return { premium: roundPremium(premium) };\n    }\n    const items = policyItems.get(step.policy)!;\n    const result = claim(items, step.incident, remainingCaps.get(step.policy));\n    remainingCaps.set(step.policy, result.remainingCap);\n    return { payout: roundPayout(result.payout), remainingCap: result.remainingCap };\n  });\n\n  return { results };\n};","oldText":"export const processScenario = (input: unknown): unknown => {\n  return undefined;\n};"}],"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24